  "info": {
   "title": "CheapVerifier API",
   "version": "1.0.0",
   "description": "Verify one email address in real time, or upload a list and verify it in bulk.\n\n## Authentication\n\nSend your key in the `x-api-key` header on every request. Create one in the dashboard under **Settings → API**.\n\n```\nx-api-key: sk_live_...\n```\n\nA key belongs to a **workspace**, not to the person who created it — so it keeps working after they leave, and it can never reach another workspace's data.\n\n## Credits\n\n**One credit per verdict.** An address that comes back `valid` or `invalid` costs 1. `catch_all` and `unknown` cost nothing, because neither is an answer about the address. There are no mode multipliers.\n\nA bulk file **holds** one credit per deduplicated row up front, so work cannot start that the workspace cannot pay for, and settles down to the rows that reached a verdict when it finishes. A workspace that cannot cover a file is refused with `402` before any address is queued.\n\n## Versioning\n\nThe version is in the path. A future `/v2` mounts alongside `/v1` rather than replacing it, so an integration built today keeps working when one arrives.\n\n## Errors\n\nFailures carry the same envelope, with the human-readable reason in both keys:\n\n```json\n{ \"success\": false, \"message\": \"…\", \"error\": \"…\" }\n```\n\nA file we cannot read is a `400` that says why — an unsupported extension, or no column of addresses. It is never a `500`."
  },
